;; Root and its procs (new in next: v1's root was a JVM with other bounds).
;; Each entry's :default is its shipped value, with its unit,
;; provenance and what happens at its bound in the comment above it; a value read from the process (#env, a path
;; under the checkout, a #profile choice) is resources/seon/config/default.edn's (docs/config.md#layers).
{:seon.config.root/profile [:keyword {:seon.config/place true :seon.config/unit "profile" :description "The aero profile this process read the config file under (--profile NAME on its command line, else :default): recorded, never set by a file; `#profile` values in default.edn vary by it (docs/config.md#layers)."}]
 ;; Unit: a name. The one person this store's boot makes as its user (:seon.user/name) and signs in (:seon.system/signed-in), until there
 ;; is a login; a person sets their own in config/local.edn ({:seon.config.root/user-name "sean"}). Provenance: replaced the OS
 ;; account read at boot (seon.system/person), owner's ruling via the managing session, 2026-11-10: a default in the config file is
 ;; config, not a fake default in code.
 :seon.config.root/user-name [:string {:default "user" :min 1 :seon.config/unit "name" :description "The one person's name, the user entity a fresh store's boot makes and signs in (:seon.user/name, :seon.system/signed-in), until there is a login."}]
 ;; Unit: ms. A seon_inbox call's wait for a message, then :seon.server/no-message and the session asks again. Provenance: root's
 ;; ruling 2026-11-15 (600000, an outside client's bound; its sender is often a person or another session).
 :seon.config.root/inbox-wait-ms [:int {:default 600000 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "ms" :description "How long a seon_inbox call waits for a message before it answers :seon.server/no-message: an outside client's bound (a session's MCP call), since a message's sender is often a person or another session (the world outside). The session asks again."}]
 ;; Provenance: flow, 2026-11-15 (root's ask): four tests stopped at their 300 s bound waiting on a shared root's quiet; only a
 ;; shard's shared root sets it (seon.test-store/start-shared-root!), every other root is a root of its own
 :seon.config.root/shared [:boolean {:default false :seon.config/unit "flag" :description "Whether this root is a test shard's shared root (seon.test-store/start-shared-root! sets it), whose tests run one after another on one root: whole-root quiet there waits on every other test's leftovers, so seon.await/await-quiet answers :seon.await/shared-root naming await-db. E removes it with the shared roots, once tests fork from the standing system."}]
 :seon.config.root/max-agents [:int {:seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "agents" :description "Live agents at most; a spawn past it is refused (root holds a socket per agent)."}]
 ;; Unit: bytes. How much of a dead agent's stderr its death records: the last bytes of its
 ;; file. Provenance: the value seon.system held as a literal (shrink). At the bound: earlier
 ;; output is not recorded; the file itself is kept.
 :seon.config.root/death-stderr-bytes [:int {:default 2048 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "bytes" :description "How much of a dead agent's stderr its death records: the last bytes of its file (seon.lib/tail-bytes)."}]
 ;; Unit: ms. Flow's :stop-timeout-ms for root's graph (seon.system/start!). Provenance: the literal
 ;; 10000 it replaces. At the bound: flow/stop answers the pids still running.
 :seon.config.root/stop-ms [:int {:default 3000 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "ms" :description "The one bound of a root's stop, for each of its two parts: its drain (the stop fact and every proc's drain, seon.system/stop!) and Flow's stop of the graph (its :stop-timeout-ms). A drain past it answers the typed :seon.system/stop-overran naming what was held, and the stop goes on. The root prints the whole, both parts (seon.system/stop-bound-ms), on its ROOT LISTENING line, and bin/system stop kills it only past that (bin/held --end's deadline), taking its evidence first. Default 10x the slowest of 12 measured clean exits of an idle root (0.19-0.29 s, 2026-11-14)."}]
 ;; Unit: entries. The newest entries root's view keeps of a list it grows: an agent's
 ;; evaluations and root's own defects; the view counts them all, and a render says how many it
 ;; left. Provenance: the value seon.system held as a literal twice (shrink). At the bound: the
 ;; oldest entry leaves the view; the facts on main keep everything.
 :seon.config.root/view-window [:int {:default 20 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "entries" :description "The newest entries root's view keeps of a list it grows (an agent's evaluations, root's own defects); the view counts them all."}]
 ;; Unit: writer requests from the api in flight. Provenance: f2-final. At the bound the api
 ;; stops reading its server (Flow's input filter) and reads only answers, so callers are
 ;; pushed back and the writer's answers always have room: the api <-> writer cycle cannot wedge.
 :seon.config.root/api-writes [:int {:default 512 :seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "requests" :description "Writer requests from the api in flight at most; at the bound the api reads only answers."}]
 ;; Unit: messages one api step takes before it applies its graph change (spawns and ends
 ;; become one update!). Provenance: f2-final. At the bound: the step ends and the rest wait.
 :seon.config.root/api-batch [:int {:default 256 :min 1 :seon.config/unit "messages" :description "Most messages one api step takes before applying its graph change."}]
 ;; Unit: requests one writer step drains and commits together (group commit). Provenance:
 ;; f2-final. At the bound: the next step takes the rest.
 :seon.config.root/writer-batch [:int {:default 256 :seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "requests" :description "Most requests one writer step drains and commits together (group commit)."}]
 :seon.config.root/writer-buf [:int {:seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "requests" :description "The writer's in-port; beyond it senders park."}]
 :seon.config.root/wiki-baseline [:boolean {:seon.config/place true :seon.config/unit "on/off" :description "Whether a load of the wiki takes, for each section with no record of the code it was written against, that record from git (the commit that last changed the section; seon.doc/baseline-reads). Off: such a section is recorded as of today."}]
 ;; Unit: main's commits queued for the reconciler. It reads every commit's datoms (an index
 ;; kept by observing them), so the buffer blocks rather than drops: at the bound the writer's
 ;; send parks until the reconciler catches up (a pass costs what the commit changed).
 :seon.config.root/reconciler-buf [:int {:default 1024 :seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "commits" :description "Main's commits queued for the reconciler; a full buffer parks the writer."}]
 :seon.config.root/runs-dir [:string {:seon.config/optional true :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "Where kept runs live (never deleted)."}]
 :seon.config.root/store-path [:string {:seon.config/optional true :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "The one store every root works in, on its own main branch."}]
 :seon.config.root/main [:string {:seon.config/optional true :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "branch" :description "Root's main branch, resumed at every boot; made from :db when the store has none."}]
 ;; Unit: directories of the checkout ("." is its top level, the .md files there: AGENTS.md, BAGGAGE.md,
 ;; README.md). The pages an index (a seed, or my.root/load-docs!) writes into main as wiki sections
 ;; (seon.system/wiki-tx), so one search and one view reach them (owner, 2026-10-27: "everything of
 ;; consequence that is for seon agents use should be indexed into the db"); a boot reads none.
 ;; Provenance: one-index audit, step 6 (root's scratchpad one-index.md). At the
 ;; bound: n/a; a dir with no .md files loads nothing.
 :seon.config.root/wiki-dirs [:vector {:default ["docs" "."] :seon.config/unit "directories" :description "The directories of the checkout whose .md files root loads into main as wiki sections at boot (docs/ is also watched); \".\" is the checkout's top level."} [:string {:min 1}]]
 :seon.config.root/tasks-dir [:string {:seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "The task files seon.system/task-files reads: a place, each root's own (a test root's is under its runs, seon.test-store/start-root!), so it is no input of a test's result."}]
 ;; Unit: percent, the most of root's heap kept free after a full collection (Jolt's
 ;; JOLT_MAX_HEAP_FREE_RATIO, the JVM's -XX:MaxHeapFreeRatio: P% free is P/(100-P) of the heap in
 ;; use), set after the fork server is forked (seon.lib/max-heap-free-ratio!), so the fork server and
 ;; agents keep Jolt's default 50; it bounds root's nursery headroom over the live set by the same share. Root collects in full at
 ;; boot and at each quiescence (the writer's :collect), which is when Chez returns pages.
 ;; Provenance: jolt/root-reserve-cap (Jolt's default 50 kept 1x, 234-450 MB free in an idle
 ;; root). At the bound: 1 returns nearly every free page and keeps the nursery at its floor.
 :seon.config.root/max-heap-free-ratio [:int {:default 10 :seon.config/at-load true :min 1 :max 99 :seon.config/unit "percent" :description "The most of root's heap kept free after a full collection (Jolt's JOLT_MAX_HEAP_FREE_RATIO, the JVM's -XX:MaxHeapFreeRatio); the rest goes back to the OS."}]
 ;; Unit: generations. Chez's maximum generation, set by root at its boot before its first fork (jolt.host/gc-generations!).
 ;; Each level of forks collects one generation less than its parent (Jolt: a forked child never collects what it inherited,
 ;; task jolt.host/a-forked-child-never-collects-what-it-inherited): root, the fork server, an agent, a test child and a
 ;; double-forked clone are five levels: 6, the most our Chez supports (measured 2026-11-16: 8 is refused, "exceeds maximum
 ;; supported value 6"), leaves the fork server 0-5, an agent 0-4, a test child 0-3 and a clone 0-2.
 :seon.config.root/gc-generations [:int {:default 6 :seon.config/at-load true :min 4 :max 6 :seon.config/unit "generations" :description "Chez's maximum generation, set by root before its first fork: each level of forks collects one generation less than its parent, so it bounds how deep forks may go and still collect."}]
 ;; Unit: threads, Chez's parallel-collector sweepers in root, fixed at boot right after the
 ;; fork server is forked (seon.lib/gc-sweepers!; seon.main/-main fixed the pool at 0 before that, so the
 ;; fork server never has one). 0: root collects on the thread that triggers
 ;; it. Provenance: session THREADS, 2026-10-21: unfixed, Chez kept one per thread a collection
 ;; found waiting, so root's count drifted with load (0, 5, 15 across identical runs); A/B at
 ;; 0/2/4/8 gave the same GC real time, GC CPU rising with n, threads 37/39/41/45. At the bound: none.
 :seon.config.root/gc-sweepers [:int {:default 0 :seon.config/at-load true :min 0 :seon.config/unit "threads" :description "Chez parallel-collector sweepers in root, fixed at boot after the fork server is forked; 0: collect on the triggering thread."}]}
